  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNFPA Improved access to SRHR for youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to UNFPA&apos;s country programme in Madagascar with a particular focus on adolescents and young people&apos;s  rights to sexual and reproductive health information and services, particularly of comprehensive sexuality education, leadership skills and resilience building. The project will focus on four key areas; 1) access to quality youth-friendly ASRH services including EmONC/ FP /STIs and HIV and GBV, 2)  institutional capacity to transform policies and sustain financing, 3) youth leadership and advocacy on ASRH, 4) capacities of actors and institutions to address discriminatory and social norms to advance SRHR of adolescents.</narrative>
  </description>
